IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sge-p10a-355-356`

-- Tests of ss 355 and 356 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration). Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the
-- assertion, before the run; none is copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Section 355: this Part applies to a foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered`

-- "This Part applies to a foreign corporate entity which intends to be registered as a company limited by shares under this Act."
-- Both limbs met: yes. Either limb missing: the text speaks only of an entity of that kind, so it says nothing (NOTHING, scope limit).
#ASSERT `s 355 this Part applies to the body` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 355 this Part applies to the body` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 355 this Part applies to the body` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 355 this Part applies to the body` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 356: the opening words, "unless the context otherwise requires"`

-- A word the section defines, used where the context does not require otherwise: the definition governs.
#ASSERT `s 356 the definition in this section governs the word where it is used` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the context otherwise requires": where it does, the text says no in its own words.
#ASSERT `s 356 the definition in this section governs the word where it is used` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A word the section does not define: the opening words say nothing about it.
#ASSERT `s 356 the definition in this section governs the word where it is used` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 356 the definition in this section governs the word where it is used` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 356: "date of registration"`

-- The date is the one "specified in the notice of transfer of registration", for an entity that has applied. Notice dated 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 3 2027)
-- Applied, but no notice yet: no date is specified, so the definition gives none.
#ASSERT `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not applied: defined only "in relation to a foreign corporate entity that has applied".
#ASSERT `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE TRUE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 356 "date of registration" the date of registration of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2027) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 356: "foreign corporate entity"`

-- "means a body corporate that is incorporated outside Singapore": both limbs, or it is not one (a "means" definition).
#ASSERT `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 356 "foreign corporate entity" the body is a foreign corporate entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 356: "notice of transfer of registration"`

-- "means the notice of transfer of registration issued under section 359(3)".
#ASSERT `s 356 "notice of transfer of registration" the notice is the notice of transfer of registration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 356 "notice of transfer of registration" the notice is the notice of transfer of registration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 356: "place of incorporation"`

-- For an entity that transferred its domicile after incorporation: the jurisdiction where it is domiciled when it applies.
#ASSERT `s 356 "place of incorporation" the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE "Cayman Islands" EQUALS JUST "Cayman Islands"
-- For any other entity the definition is silent.
#ASSERT `s 356 "place of incorporation" the place of incorporation of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE "Cayman Islands" EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 356: "registration", "register" and "registered"`

-- "registration" means registration by the Registrar under section 359(1), for an entity that has applied.
#ASSERT `s 356 "registration" the act is registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 356 "registration" the act is registration of the foreign corporate entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An entity that has not applied: the definition is not given for it.
#ASSERT `s 356 "registration" the act is registration of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 356 "registration" the act is registration of the foreign corporate entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "register" and "registered" are "construed accordingly".
#ASSERT `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 356 "register" and "registered" the foreign corporate entity is registered` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
